  <h1>Boiler Advice for Holgate Homeowners</h1>
  <p>We've covered Holgate for 18 years, right next door to our base in Acomb — so whichever part of the area you're in, chances are we've already worked a few streets away. This page brings together what Holgate homeowners ask us most: what things cost, how to check you're getting a proper Gas Safe engineer, and what to do the moment the heating goes off.</p>

  <h2>How much does a new boiler cost in Holgate?</h2>
  <p>A like-for-like combi swap starts from £2,000; a system-to-combi conversion (where more pipework is involved) starts from £3,000. Most Holgate jobs fall between £2,000 and £3,000, depending on the boiler and the property. We always give you a free, written quote before anything's agreed — no pressure to buy bigger than you need.</p>
  <p>See our <a href="/new-boiler-installation-holgate/">New Boiler Installation in Holgate</a> page for pricing, or read our <a href="/advice-centre/new-boiler-cost/">full cost breakdown</a> and <a href="/advice-centre/combi-vs-system-boiler/">combi vs system guide</a> if you're not sure which boiler type suits your home.</p>

  <h2>Finding a Gas Safe engineer in Holgate</h2>
  <p>Whoever you use, check their Gas Safe registration number on the official register first — it's a legal requirement, and it takes thirty seconds. We're registered under 570248, and Worcester Bosch and Ideal accredited, which matters for keeping your manufacturer's warranty valid. A good number of the calls that come in start with someone who's been let down by a previous engineer, sometimes more than once — it's one of the most common things we hear, and it's an easy one to fix.</p>

  <h2>Boiler breakdowns — what to do first</h2>
  <p>No heating or hot water is our most common call across the whole of York, and it's usually a pressure, valve, or PCB issue that gets sorted in one visit. Start by checking the pressure gauge — anything under 1 bar points to a leak or a recent radiator bleed. If there's an error code showing, tell us what it says when you ring; it often tells us most of what we need before we've even set off.</p>
  <p>A good number of our emergency calls aren't even for the person ringing — it's someone checking on an elderly relative, or a new parent who doesn't want the house going cold overnight. Tell us if that's the situation and we'll treat it as the priority it is.</p>
  <p>Our <a href="/boiler-repairs-holgate/">Boiler Repairs &amp; Breakdowns in Holgate</a> page has our current call-out pricing, and our <a href="/advice-centre/why-is-my-boiler-losing-pressure/">pressure troubleshooting guide</a> covers what's safe to check yourself before you call.</p>

  <h2>Don't wait for it to break — get it serviced</h2>
  <p>An annual service is £100 + VAT and it's the simplest way to avoid an emergency callout — it also protects your manufacturer's warranty, which most homeowners only discover has lapsed when it's too late. If you're a landlord anywhere in Holgate, this is also where your CP12 gas safety certificate comes from; see our <a href="/gas-safety-landlords/">Gas Safety &amp; Landlords</a> page for the full legal requirement.</p>
  <p>If you'd rather not think about it every year, our <a href="/boiler-care-plans/">Boiler Care Plans</a> start from £12.99/month and include your annual service, and a free CO alarm.</p>

  <h2>Book a Holgate visit</h2>
  <p>Whether you need a new boiler quote, an urgent repair, or your annual service, we cover Holgate and the surrounding area. Call us and tell us what's going on — you'll get a straight answer, not a sales pitch.</p>
